 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Cross-Guided Optimization of Radiance Fields (CROP)](10371-cross-guided-optimization-of-radiance-fields-crop.md)
-CROP performs multi-view image super-resolution (MVSR) on training-view images during the radiance field optimization process to improve high-resolution novel view synthesis (HRNVS). It addresses the limitation that standard radiance fields rely heavily on the spectral characteristics of coordinate-based networks, which restricts their ability to synthesize high-frequency details independently. By fusing single-image super-resolution (SISR) features with voxel-based uncertainty fields derived from rendering errors, CROP ensures multi-view consistency and high-frequency detail in the training images, which are then used to refine the radiance field.
+CROP performs multi-view image super-resolution (MVSR) on training-view images during the radiance field optimization process to improve high-resolution novel view synthesis (HRNVS). It addresses the limitation that standard radiance fields rely heavily on the spectral characteristics of coordinate-based networks, which restricts their ability to synthesize high-frequency details independently. By fusing single-image super-resolution (SISR) features with voxel-based uncertainty fields derived from rendering errors, CROP ensures multi-view consistency and high-frequency detail in the training images, which are then used to refine the radiance field. Choose it when high-frequency detail recovery is needed despite MLP spectral bias.
 
