 ### [Urban Radiance Fields](11973-urban-radiance-fields.md)
-Urban Radiance Fields applies NeRF to urban environments using sparse multi-view images supplemented by LiDAR data. It addresses the challenges of unbounded outdoor scenes, limited camera pose variety, and large-scale scene requirements by integrating geometric priors from LiDAR into the optimization loop. Unlike standard NeRF which relies solely on photometric consistency, this method enforces geometric accuracy and semantic consistency through specific depth, sight, and segmentation losses.
+Urban Radiance Fields applies NeRF to urban environments using sparse multi-view images supplemented by LiDAR data. It addresses the challenges of unbounded outdoor scenes, limited camera pose variety, and large-scale scene requirements by integrating geometric priors from LiDAR into the optimization loop. Unlike standard NeRF which relies solely on photometric consistency, this method enforces geometric accuracy and semantic consistency through specific depth, sight, and segmentation losses. Choose it for large-scale outdoor reconstruction with LiDAR priors.
 
 ### [RehearsalNeRF](12477-rehearsalnerf.md)
-RehearsalNeRF learns disentangled neural fields in scenes with severe, dynamic illumination changes by leveraging a "rehearsal stage" (captured under stable lighting) to enforce geometric consistency. It solves the "illumination-radiance ambiguity" where dynamic lighting effects are entangled with object radiance, a problem not addressed by methods assuming stable light sources. Unlike [Urban Radiance Fields](11973-urban-radiance-fields.md) which handles geometric priors, RehearsalNeRF explicitly decouples dynamic illuminations, static objects, and dynamic objects into five separate neural fields, enabling applications like controlling lighting while stopping motion.
+RehearsalNeRF learns disentangled neural fields in scenes with severe, dynamic illumination changes by leveraging a "rehearsal stage" (captured under stable lighting) to enforce geometric consistency. It solves the "illumination-radiance ambiguity" where dynamic lighting effects are entangled with object radiance, a problem not addressed by methods assuming stable light sources. Unlike [Urban Radiance Fields](11973-urban-radiance-fields.md) which handles geometric priors, RehearsalNeRF explicitly decouples dynamic illuminations, static objects, and dynamic objects into five separate neural fields, enabling applications like controlling lighting while stopping motion. Choose it for dynamic scenes with changing illumination.
 
 ### [Neural SAR Surface Reconstruction via Inverse Rendering](12668-neural-sar-surface-reconstruction-via-inverse-rendering.md)
-This method reconstructs a Digital Surface Model (DSM) and a backscattering coefficient map from Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) images by minimizing the difference between observed SAR intensities and synthesized intensities using a differentiable rendering model. It models elevation $Z$ and backscattering $B$ within a bounding box using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP), reducing sampling degrees of freedom from a 3D volume to a 2D surface. Unlike standard NeRF which optimizes a 3D density field, this approach enforces surface constraints by mapping 2D ground coordinates directly to elevation and appearance, leading to faster and easier reconstruction of surfaces.
+This method reconstructs a Digital Surface Model (DSM) and a backscattering coefficient map from Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) images by minimizing the difference between observed SAR intensities and synthesized intensities using a differentiable rendering model. It models elevation $Z$ and backscattering $B$ within a bounding box using a Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP), reducing sampling degrees of freedom from a 3D volume to a 2D surface. Unlike standard NeRF which optimizes a 3D density field, this approach enforces surface constraints by mapping 2D ground coordinates directly to elevation and appearance, leading to faster and easier reconstruction of surfaces. Choose it for SAR data reconstruction.
 
 ### [360FusionNeRF](12755-360fusionnerf.md)
-360FusionNeRF is a semi-supervised learning framework for synthesizing novel views from a single RGB-D 360° panorama image. It extends OmniNeRF by introducing geometric supervision via auxiliary depth maps and semantic consistency via CLIP features to guide progressive training and reduce artifacts caused by occlusion in unobserved regions. Unlike standard NeRF methods that rely solely on photometric reconstruction, 360FusionNeRF explicitly constrains the geometry and semantics of the learned radiance field to ensure plausible completions of missing data.
+360FusionNeRF is a semi-supervised learning framework for synthesizing novel views from a single RGB-D 360° panorama image. It extends OmniNeRF by introducing geometric supervision via auxiliary depth maps and semantic consistency via CLIP features to guide progressive training and reduce artifacts caused by occlusion in unobserved regions. Unlike standard NeRF methods that rely solely on photometric reconstruction, 360FusionNeRF explicitly constrains the geometry and semantics of the learned radiance field to ensure plausible completions of missing data. Choose it for single-panorama novel view synthesis.
 
 ### [Portrait-NeRF](13429-portrait-nerf.md)
-Portrait-NeRF estimates Neural Radiance Fields from a single headshot portrait image. It addresses the ill-posed nature of training an MLP from a single image by pretraining the MLP with a meta-learning framework on a light stage dataset and finetuning it on the input image. Unlike standard NeRF which requires multiple views, or 3D model-based methods that exclude upper head and torso, Portrait-NeRF reconstructs the full portrait including hairs and accessories using a canonical coordinate warping strategy.
+Portrait-NeRF estimates Neural Radiance Fields from a single headshot portrait image. It addresses the ill-posed nature of training an MLP from a single image by pretraining the MLP with a meta-learning framework on a light stage dataset and finetuning it on the input image. Unlike standard NeRF which requires multiple views, or 3D model-based methods that exclude upper head and torso, Portrait-NeRF reconstructs the full portrait including hairs and accessories using a canonical coordinate warping strategy. Choose it for single-image portrait synthesis.
 
 ### [Mirror-NeRF](13482-mirror-nerf.md)
-Mirror-NeRF is a neural rendering framework that learns accurate mirror geometry and reflection by unifying the radiance field and tracing rays according to Whitted-style light transport, enabling novel view synthesis and scene manipulation. Unlike NeRF and NeRFReN, which treat mirror reflections as separate virtual scenes or interpolate memorized reflections, Mirror-NeRF uses a unified radiance field with explicit reflection probability and Whitted-style ray tracing to synthesize physically consistent reflections from novel viewpoints.
